# docs/

This directory holds the documentation of this collection. Kephalaion indexes it for
assistants that read it through MCP, the tools of a Kephalaion node. Content in `docs/` is
English.

## Three questions, three ways

- **What is here?** Read the `index.md` of a directory with `read`. It lists the
  subdirectories and documents of exactly that level, each with its title and a one-sentence
  description. Start with `docs/index.md`.
- **Where is X?** Use `search` with plain English words; questions work. A hit is a section of a
  document: pass its `name` and its `anchor` to `read` (as `section`) to read just that part.
- **What is new?** Use `changes` with `path: docs/`.

## Generated files: do not edit

`docs/README.md` (this file) and every `index.md` below `docs/` are written by Kephalaion only,
whenever `docs/` is rebuilt (`rebuild_docs`). Writing them is refused with `generated_file`,
for the admin as well; a rebuild overwrites them.

