Below these, the structure belongs to you.

## README.md per directory

Every directory below `docs/` should have a `README.md` with front matter: `title` and
`description` (one sentence). The index shows both. Where it is missing, a rebuild puts a
notice in its place. Replace the notice with `write` (not `create`, the name is taken); anyone
with `write` may.

## Front matter of a document

`title`, `description` (one sentence), and optionally `questions` (questions this document
answers; they weigh high in search), `hints`, `sources`, `verified`, and `generated` for
generated documents.

## Keeping the index current

There is no automatic rebuild yet. After changing `docs/`, call `rebuild_docs` for the
collection. Until then `index.md` may be out of date, and a directory that was renamed has no
`index.md`.
